    "https://www.moreheadstate.edu/student-support/career-ready/index": {
      "title": "Career-Ready Experience",
      "description": "Career-Ready Experience | Morehead State University | Kentucky Skip Menu Menu Info For Current Students Future Students Craft Academy Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Parents & Families Community & Business Quicklinks MyMoreheadState Manage Your Account Blackboard Canvas Email Library Calendar of Events Search for Courses/Sections University Bookstore A-Z Guide Athletics Go Academics Explore Academic Programs Colleges & Departments Graduate Programs Online Programs Craft Academy for Excellence in Science & Mathematics George M. Luckey Academic Honors Program Academic Affairs & Provost Camden-Carroll Library Instructional Design & Online Learning Research Support & Success Career Prep Education Abroad Internships Level UP Service Learning Undergraduate Research Advising & Tutoring Essential Needs & Aid Student Accessibility Services Wellness & Emergency Resources Admissions & Aid Apply to MSU Transfer Eagle Scholars (Dual Credit) International Students Veteran & Military-Connected Students Financial Aid Scholarships Tuition & Fees Meet the Eagles - Student Stories Schedule a Visit Virtual Tour Student Life Activities & Organizations Athletics Housing Recreation & Wellness Center Dean of Students Eagle Student Handbook Campus Safety Student Center & Conference Services About MSU At-a-Glance History Mission & Vision Accreditation News Rankings Campus Map Emergency Resources Leadership Campus Revitalization Community & Business Contact Us Email Us! Home Students Career-Ready Experience Section Menu Student Support Career-Ready Home Alumni Info Faculty & Staff Resources Employer Info Level UP: Skills that SOAR! Explore Majors & Careers Career & Internship Fair Career Guide Market Yourself Education Abroad Internships Level UP Service Learning Student Research Experiential Education Fund Awards Staff Advising & Tutoring College Readiness Student Accessibility Services Academic Honors Program Career-Ready Experience MSU’s Center for Career Development & Experiential Education (CCDEE) helps you create your future. We are committed to cultivating a network of and supporting students, alumni, faculty, and employers through a comprehensive approach to career development. Award-Winning Career Support MSU is nationally recognized as a 2025–26 College of Distinction for Career Development—because students succeed here. This honor reflects our commitment to helping you gain a competitive edge through hands-on experience, personalized guidance, and career-focused resources. See More Rankings & Honors Real-World Experience Starts Here Experiential education, including internships , service learning , education abroad programs , and undergraduate research , is a cornerstone of our mission to empower students to develop in-demand skills needed for success in the professional world. We help you explore major and career options , plan the experiences you need to build career skills and learn to market yourself to potential employers and graduate schools. Career & Internship Fair MSU hosts two career fairs annually. These events bring 100+ employers and graduate programs to campus. Attend the next fair on Sep. 30, 2026, from 10 a.m. to 1 p.m. in the ADUC Ballroom to meet employers and find internship opportunities. Learn More Explore Careers & Majors Explore Careers & Majors Get help finding your major or career. Build Career Skills Build Career Skills Gain the skills that employers are looking for in employees. Market Yourself Market Yourself Get help with resumes, interviews, networking and more. Explore Opportunities with Eagle CareerNet The MSU's Eagle CareerNet portal helps you find job and internship opportunities, connect with employers and create your career plan. Go Eagle CareerNet Career Guide Your guide to career planning, resume and interviewing preparation, and finding a job or internship. View the Guide Expand Your Experience Pursue the real-world experience employers look for in job candidates. Research and creative work, community service, education abroad, and other activities will make you a stronger job candidate and make your MSU experience unforgettable. Education Abroad Education Abroad Earn credits, explore languages and cultures, and make memories. Internships Internships Gain real workplace experience while earning credits. Level UP Level UP Gain a competitive edge with career-oriented courses, faculty mentoring, and hands-on experience. Service Learning Service Learning Help communities while building practical experience. Student Research Student Research Develop ideas and innovations with faculty mentors and peers. Experiential Education Awards Experiential Education Awards Recognition for students, faculty, staff and community partners for their work. Employer Info Find out how to connect with students and alumni, and more. Faculty & Staff Info Find resources to help students with career planning and skills. Alumni Info Get help with your career planning and connect with students and other alumni. CCDEE News Harr honored with Martin Visionary Award Harr honored with Martin Visionary Award Kentucky Commercialization Ventures presented Dr. Shannon Harr (Class of 1999, 2001) with the Thomas M. Martin Visionary A... Morehead State students recognized for community service Morehead State students recognized for community service More than 100 MSU students were named Spring 2026 Presidential Community Engaged Eagles for service-learning projects and ... Morehead State’s Alexis Mathews Selected for Nation... Morehead State’s Alexis Mathews Selected for Nation... MSU’s Alexis Mathews elected Division Representative for the Council on Undergraduate Research, advancing undergradu... Career Events SEE MORE MSU EVENTS Contact Us Center for Career Development & Experiential Education Ground floor, Camden-Carroll Library 150 University Blvd. Morehead, KY 40351 HOURS: 8 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. EMAIL: careerservices@moreheadstate.edu PHONE: 606-783-2233 Apply Now Visit MSU Get More Info 150 University Blvd. Morehead, Kentucky 40351 1-800-585-6781 606-783-2000 Academic Catalogs Academic Calendars Accreditation Transcripts Privacy Policy Nondiscrimination & Title IX Web Accessibility MAKE A GIFT SEARCH JOB POSTINGS © 2026 Morehead State University"
