    "https://www.moreheadstate.edu/student-support/career-ready/education-abroad/index": {
      "title": "Education Abroad",
      "description": "Education Abroad | Morehead State University | Kentucky Skip Menu Menu Info For Current Students Future Students Craft Academy Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Parents & Families Community & Business Quicklinks MyMoreheadState Manage Your Account Blackboard Canvas Email Library Calendar of Events Search for Courses/Sections University Bookstore A-Z Guide Athletics Go Academics Explore Academic Programs Colleges & Departments Graduate Programs Online Programs Craft Academy for Excellence in Science & Mathematics George M. Luckey Academic Honors Program Academic Affairs & Provost Camden-Carroll Library Instructional Design & Online Learning Research Support & Success Career Prep Education Abroad Internships Level UP Service Learning Undergraduate Research Advising & Tutoring Essential Needs & Aid Student Accessibility Services Wellness & Emergency Resources Admissions & Aid Apply to MSU Transfer Eagle Scholars (Dual Credit) International Students Veteran & Military-Connected Students Financial Aid Scholarships Tuition & Fees Meet the Eagles - Student Stories Schedule a Visit Virtual Tour Student Life Activities & Organizations Athletics Housing Recreation & Wellness Center Dean of Students Eagle Student Handbook Campus Safety Student Center & Conference Services About MSU At-a-Glance History Mission & Vision Accreditation News Rankings Campus Map Emergency Resources Leadership Campus Revitalization Community & Business Contact Us Email Us! Home Students Career-Ready Home Education Abroad Section Menu Career-Ready Experience Alumni Info Faculty & Staff Resources Employer Info Level UP: Skills that SOAR! Explore Majors & Careers Career & Internship Fair Career Guide Market Yourself Education Abroad Programs Student Resources Scholarships Faculty Resources Internships Level UP Service Learning Student Research Experiential Education Fund Awards Staff Education Abroad Experience different cultures and learn about the world through short- or long-term experiences, as well as internship opportunities in other countries. Traveling the World Learn from several of our students from Kentucky and across the country who share their experiences overseas and what studying abroad has done for them. Watch Video Studying abroad expands your horizons—literally. You’ll discover new cultures, cities, and scenery and gain a new sense of what’s possible. It is more than a trip, as programs are designed to use the location to help you learn the course material. MSU participates in various collaborative exchange agreements and consortia memberships where you can earn academic credit for academic experiences abroad. Study at an international university for a few weeks in the summer, winter, or during the week of spring break. You can spend a full semester or a whole year overseas. Scholarships for education abroad or other financial aid can help cover your costs. Make A Plan With dozens of destinations, short- and long-term schedules, and scholarships available, there’s a study abroad option for virtually every student. To make your plan: Explore available programs. Complete our student interest form . Talk to the education abroad coordinator about your options. Apply for financial aid or scholarships . Consult resources about international travel, health, and other considerations. \"I had the opportunity to work with passionate educators and enthusiastic students, which was incredibly fulfilling.\" - Regarding her experience student-teaching in Belfast Erikah Voll Elementary Education Major from Salyersville Read more about Erikah's experience Programs Programs Learn about opportunities to study or teach abroad. Scholarships Scholarships Learn about financial aid that can help you study abroad. Student Resources Student Resources Get information about the process and what you'll need to study abroad. Faculty Resources Faculty Resources Get information and resources about teaching abroad. Interested in Education Abroad? Complete this form and we'll help you find the best program for you. Complete Interest Form Career Events SEE MORE MSU EVENTS CCDEE News Harr honored with Martin Visionary Award Harr honored with Martin Visionary Award Kentucky Commercialization Ventures presented Dr. Shannon Harr (Class of 1999, 2001) with the Thomas M. Martin Visionary A... Morehead State students recognized for community service Morehead State students recognized for community service More than 100 MSU students were named Spring 2026 Presidential Community Engaged Eagles for service-learning projects and ... Morehead State’s Alexis Mathews Selected for Nation... Morehead State’s Alexis Mathews Selected for Nation... MSU’s Alexis Mathews elected Division Representative for the Council on Undergraduate Research, advancing undergradu... Contact Education Abroad Dr. Jason M. Adkins Education Abroad Coordinator/Instructor Camden-Carroll Library Morehead, KY 40351 EMAIL: jm.adkins@moreheadstate.edu PHONE: 606-783-2044 Apply Now Visit MSU Get More Info 150 University Blvd. Morehead, Kentucky 40351 1-800-585-6781 606-783-2000 Academic Catalogs Academic Calendars Accreditation Transcripts Privacy Policy Nondiscrimination & Title IX Web Accessibility MAKE A GIFT SEARCH JOB POSTINGS © 2026 Morehead State University"
