    "https://www.moreheadstate.edu/student-support/career-ready/internships": {
      "title": "Internships",
      "description": "Internships | Morehead State University | Kentucky Skip Menu Menu Info For Current Students Future Students Craft Academy Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Parents & Families Community & Business Quicklinks MyMoreheadState Manage Your Account Blackboard Canvas Email Library Calendar of Events Search for Courses/Sections University Bookstore A-Z Guide Athletics Go Academics Explore Academic Programs Colleges & Departments Graduate Programs Online Programs Craft Academy for Excellence in Science & Mathematics George M. Luckey Academic Honors Program Academic Affairs & Provost Camden-Carroll Library Instructional Design & Online Learning Research Support & Success Career Prep Education Abroad Internships Level UP Service Learning Undergraduate Research Advising & Tutoring Essential Needs & Aid Student Accessibility Services Wellness & Emergency Resources Admissions & Aid Apply to MSU Transfer Eagle Scholars (Dual Credit) International Students Veteran & Military-Connected Students Financial Aid Scholarships Tuition & Fees Meet the Eagles - Student Stories Schedule a Visit Virtual Tour Student Life Activities & Organizations Athletics Housing Recreation & Wellness Center Dean of Students Eagle Student Handbook Campus Safety Student Center & Conference Services About MSU At-a-Glance History Mission & Vision Accreditation News Rankings Campus Map Emergency Resources Leadership Campus Revitalization Community & Business Contact Us Email Us! Home Students Career-Ready Home Internships Section Menu Career-Ready Experience Alumni Info Faculty & Staff Resources Employer Info Level UP: Skills that SOAR! Explore Majors & Careers Career & Internship Fair Career Guide Market Yourself Education Abroad Internships Level UP Service Learning Student Research Experiential Education Fund Awards Staff Internships Internships can give you the experience and connections for career success. The CCDEE can help you find an internship in your major and connect you with organizations, employers and experiences to help you develop skills for career success. “During my internship with the Legislative Research Commission, I developed a range of professional and personal skills that will be valuable throughout my career. There was a real sense of excitement in taking on complex problems that affect everyday Kentuckians, people I may never meet but know I am helping in some meaningful way.” Political Science & History Taylor Bishop Greensburg, KY Class of 2026 Why should I do an internship? Why should I get an internship or co-op Job? According to the National Association of Colleges & Employers (NACE), candidates with career-related experience receive more interviews, more job offers, and higher starting salaries than candidates without such experience. Gain experience for your resume. It helps you understand the industry and the job. Might be an entryway to a full-time job. Helps you get specialized training from the employer. How do I get an internship or co-op job? There are multiple methods to secure an internship or co-op job: Your network of faculty, staff, and past employers Eagle CareerNet Employment sites around the internet. Fill Out the Internship Interest Form Internships through MSU 339 MSU 339 is an internship program provided by Morehead State University through Career Services. This opportunity is a competency-based practical work experience that integrates theoretical aspects of education with work experience. You must have the instructor's consent, and the learning contract must be signed and submitted to Career Services before the add/drop date. You must also submit an up-to-date resume and your contract for review to Career Services. DOWNLOAD MSU 339 REQUIREMENTS AND LEARNING CONTRACT Please return the completed and signed MSU 339 learning contract and your resume to careerservices@moreheadstate.edu . Internship Opportunities 🔎 Search for internships and other experiences on Eagle CareerNet. Financial Assistance Get financial support for an experiential education opportunity like an internship, service learning, research, or education abroad. Apply for the Fund Experiential Awards CCDEE is seeking nominations for the Experiential Education Awards to recognize outstanding students, faculty/staff and employers. Make a Nomination Coordinator of Internships Rebecca Wright Center for Career Development and Experiential Education 3D Camden-Carroll Library EMAIL: ro.wright@moreheadstate.edu PHONE: 606-783-2619 Apply Now Visit MSU Get More Info 150 University Blvd. Morehead, Kentucky 40351 1-800-585-6781 606-783-2000 Academic Catalogs Academic Calendars Accreditation Transcripts Privacy Policy Nondiscrimination & Title IX Web Accessibility MAKE A GIFT SEARCH JOB POSTINGS © 2026 Morehead State University"
    },
    "https://www.moreheadstate.edu/student-support/career-ready/level-up/index": {
      "title": "Level UP",
      "description": "Level UP | Morehead State University | Kentucky Skip Menu Menu Info For Current Students Future Students Craft Academy Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Parents & Families Community & Business Quicklinks MyMoreheadState Manage Your Account Blackboard Canvas Email Library Calendar of Events Search for Courses/Sections University Bookstore A-Z Guide Athletics Go Academics Explore Academic Programs Colleges & Departments Graduate Programs Online Programs Craft Academy for Excellence in Science & Mathematics George M. Luckey Academic Honors Program Academic Affairs & Provost Camden-Carroll Library Instructional Design & Online Learning Research Support & Success Career Prep Education Abroad Internships Level UP Service Learning Undergraduate Research Advising & Tutoring Essential Needs & Aid Student Accessibility Services Wellness & Emergency Resources Admissions & Aid Apply to MSU Transfer Eagle Scholars (Dual Credit) International Students Veteran & Military-Connected Students Financial Aid Scholarships Tuition & Fees Meet the Eagles - Student Stories Schedule a Visit Virtual Tour Student Life Activities & Organizations Athletics Housing Recreation & Wellness Center Dean of Students Eagle Student Handbook Campus Safety Student Center & Conference Services About MSU At-a-Glance History Mission & Vision Accreditation News Rankings Campus Map Emergency Resources Leadership Campus Revitalization Community & Business Contact Us Email Us! Home Students Career-Ready Home Level UP Section Menu Career-Ready Experience Alumni Info Faculty & Staff Resources Employer Info Level UP: Skills that SOAR! Explore Majors & Careers Career & Internship Fair Career Guide Market Yourself Education Abroad Internships Level UP Current Students Prospective Student Info Faculty Resources Info for Families FAQ Service Learning Student Research Experiential Education Fund Awards Staff Level UP Gain a competitive edge with career-oriented courses, faculty mentoring, and hands-on experience. Experience Your Future With Level UP, you can start preparing for life after graduation from the moment you arrive at Morehead State. Choose specially designed courses that combine core concepts from your major with an added focus on career skills—oral communication, written communication, professionalism, critical thinking, and teamwork. Then develop your skills through research, education abroad, service learning, or internships. Level UP courses are open to all students who want to gain a competitive edge. \"In Fall 2025, I was enrolled in my first Level UP course that was being taught by Dr. Stephen Brigham, which had a component of undergraduate research in it with an emphasis on developing proficiency in Written Communication. At the end, I was able to come up with an extremely polished final version of my work, which not only helped me earn a distinction in Written Communication but also helped me have a reference for the future.\" LABINDRA SINGH DHAMI DARCHULA, NEPAL FINANCE Why Level UP? This program will help you stand out when applying for jobs and graduate school and give you hands-on experience in your major and key career skills. See what students and faculty have to say about the Level UP program. Watch Video Level UP Courses Learn how to find and enroll in a Level UP course—they're open to everyone. Click \"Advanced Search.\" Filter by Course Type of \"Level UP\" and the career skill most interests you. Find Courses \"What excites me most about Level UP is its intentional design. It allows me to enhance my courses while empowering students to strengthen their teamwork skills through the high-impact practice of service learning. By applying their knowledge in the real-world, students not only grow personally and professionally—they also make a meaningful difference in their communities. This kind of experience sets them apart in today’s marketplace and beyond.\" Janet Ratliff, EdD (pictured left) Department Chair Professor of Management/Entrepreneurship Info for Students Info for Students Learn how Level UP can prepare you for career success. Info for Future Students Info for Future Students See how Level UP prepares you for the next steps after graduation from the moment you enter the University. Info for Families & Guardians Info for Families & Guardians Learn why you should encourage your student to participate in Level UP. Level UP Info for Faculty Is your course a good candidate for Level UP? Learn how to identify and build a Level UP section. Help Students Level UP Contact Level UP Dr. Tim O'Brien & Megan Boone - Level UP Co-chairs 150 University Blvd. Morehead, KY EMAIL: levelup@moreheadstate.edu PHONE: 606-783-2233 Apply Now Visit MSU Get More Info 150 University Blvd. Morehead, Kentucky 40351 1-800-585-6781 606-783-2000 Academic Catalogs Academic Calendars Accreditation Transcripts Privacy Policy Nondiscrimination & Title IX Web Accessibility MAKE A GIFT SEARCH JOB POSTINGS © 2026 Morehead State University"
    },
    "https://www.moreheadstate.edu/student-support/career-ready/service-learning/index": {
      "title": "Service Learning",
      "description": "Service Learning | Morehead State University | Kentucky Skip Menu Menu Info For Current Students Future Students Craft Academy Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Parents & Families Community & Business Quicklinks MyMoreheadState Manage Your Account Blackboard Canvas Email Library Calendar of Events Search for Courses/Sections University Bookstore A-Z Guide Athletics Go Academics Explore Academic Programs Colleges & Departments Graduate Programs Online Programs Craft Academy for Excellence in Science & Mathematics George M. Luckey Academic Honors Program Academic Affairs & Provost Camden-Carroll Library Instructional Design & Online Learning Research Support & Success Career Prep Education Abroad Internships Level UP Service Learning Undergraduate Research Advising & Tutoring Essential Needs & Aid Student Accessibility Services Wellness & Emergency Resources Admissions & Aid Apply to MSU Transfer Eagle Scholars (Dual Credit) International Students Veteran & Military-Connected Students Financial Aid Scholarships Tuition & Fees Meet the Eagles - Student Stories Schedule a Visit Virtual Tour Student Life Activities & Organizations Athletics Housing Recreation & Wellness Center Dean of Students Eagle Student Handbook Campus Safety Student Center & Conference Services About MSU At-a-Glance History Mission & Vision Accreditation News Rankings Campus Map Emergency Resources Leadership Campus Revitalization Community & Business Contact Us Email Us! Home Students Career-Ready Home Service Learning Section Menu Career-Ready Experience Alumni Info Faculty & Staff Resources Employer Info Level UP: Skills that SOAR! Explore Majors & Careers Career & Internship Fair Career Guide Market Yourself Education Abroad Internships Level UP Service Learning Engaged Eagles Student Research Experiential Education Fund Awards Staff Service Learning Through service learning and engagement, students gain educational experiences that meet the goals of their academic courses, strengthen community assets and address community needs. Students involved with service learning can reflect on their experiences to gain a deeper understanding of course content and a broader appreciation of the discipline, improving critical thinking skills and an enhanced sense of values and civic responsibility. Participating faculty promotes active learning, engages students with different learning styles, add new insights to class discussion, increases public awareness of key issues and helps prepare today's students to be tomorrow's civic leaders. Undergraduate Engagement Fellowship Undergraduate Engagement Fellowship Learn how you can meet regional needs through a paid fellowship opportunity. Carnegie Community Engagement Carnegie Community Engagement Learn about MSU’s history of service learning and community engagement. Community Impact Awards Community Impact Awards Learn how you can get awarded for going above and beyond in your community. Financial Assistance Get financial support for an experiential education opportunity like an internship, service learning, research, or education abroad. Apply for the Fund Experiential Awards CCDEE is seeking nominations for the Experiential Education Awards to recognize outstanding students, faculty/staff and employers. Make a Nomination Get involved Service learning engages students in hands-on experiences through community service while they learn essential life and career skills. Students apply classroom knowledge to their communities to make an impact in the lives of others. Interested in partnering with us? Engaged Eagles The Engaged Eagles Initiative is our plan to help students get involved in service throughout their college career, building important skills and recognizing their community contributions. More Information Social Media Spotlight Have you made an impact in the community? Want to be featured in the center’s social media as part of our Student Spotlight? Fill out the form Career Events SEE MORE MSU EVENTS Contact Service Learning Andrew Sexton, Coordinator of Service Learning Camden-Carroll Library Morehead, KY 40351 EMAIL: atsexton@moreheadstate.edu PHONE: 606-783-5493 Apply Now Visit MSU Get More Info 150 University Blvd. Morehead, Kentucky 40351 1-800-585-6781 606-783-2000 Academic Catalogs Academic Calendars Accreditation Transcripts Privacy Policy Nondiscrimination & Title IX Web Accessibility MAKE A GIFT SEARCH JOB POSTINGS © 2026 Morehead State University"
    },
    "https://www.moreheadstate.edu/student-support/career-ready/student-research/index": {
      "title": "Student RESEARCH",
      "description": "Student Research | Morehead State University | Kentucky Skip Menu Menu Info For Current Students Future Students Craft Academy Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Parents & Families Community & Business Quicklinks MyMoreheadState Manage Your Account Blackboard Canvas Email Library Calendar of Events Search for Courses/Sections University Bookstore A-Z Guide Athletics Go Academics Explore Academic Programs Colleges & Departments Graduate Programs Online Programs Craft Academy for Excellence in Science & Mathematics George M. Luckey Academic Honors Program Academic Affairs & Provost Camden-Carroll Library Instructional Design & Online Learning Research Support & Success Career Prep Education Abroad Internships Level UP Service Learning Undergraduate Research Advising & Tutoring Essential Needs & Aid Student Accessibility Services Wellness & Emergency Resources Admissions & Aid Apply to MSU Transfer Eagle Scholars (Dual Credit) International Students Veteran & Military-Connected Students Financial Aid Scholarships Tuition & Fees Meet the Eagles - Student Stories Schedule a Visit Virtual Tour Student Life Activities & Organizations Athletics Housing Recreation & Wellness Center Dean of Students Eagle Student Handbook Campus Safety Student Center & Conference Services About MSU At-a-Glance History Mission & Vision Accreditation News Rankings Campus Map Emergency Resources Leadership Campus Revitalization Community & Business Contact Us Email Us! Home Students Career-Ready Home Student Research Section Menu Career-Ready Experience Alumni Info Faculty & Staff Resources Employer Info Level UP: Skills that SOAR! Explore Majors & Careers Career & Internship Fair Career Guide Market Yourself Education Abroad Internships Level UP Service Learning Student Research Undergraduate Research Fellowship Program Opportunities for Students Student Resources Faculty Resources Experiential Education Fund Awards Staff Student RESEARCH Research involvement allows students to learn career skills as they work with a faculty mentor to solve problems and create innovative solutions. At MSU, students can engage in research as early as their first year. The Council on Undergraduate Research defines undergraduate research as a “mentored investigation or creative inquiry conducted by undergraduates that seek to make a scholarly or artistic contribution to knowledge.\" “Participating in undergraduate research has allowed me to foster skills in communication, writing, and researching that I will use in my future career as a teacher.” Gwen Akers GET INVOLVED This hands-on, outside-the-classroom experience helps students build technical skills, written and oral communication skills, and critical thinking skills. Students attend conferences to network with professionals, present their research, publish their research, and build their resumes. What is research? Research systematically investigates a specific topic by collecting and analyzing data to gain new knowledge and understanding. It often involves formulating a hypothesis, designing a study, gathering information, and interpreting results to contribute to a field of study or discipline—a structured approach to exploring and answering questions about the world around us. There are many types of research, but two common types are: Applied research focuses on solving real-world problems by finding answers to specific questions, such as improving agricultural crop production or treating particular diseases or treatments. Basic research expands knowledge by seeking answers to universal, theoretical questions. For example, what are protons? Or how did the universe begin? More Information What does creative inquiry mean? Creative inquiry explores issues, objects or works by collecting and analyzing evidence. It includes combining or synthesizing existing ideas, products, or expertise in original ways to answer an open-ended question or to achieve a desired goal. There needs to be a measurable, tangible impact. Research and creative inquiry will look different depending on your goals and disciplines: Tab Information Inquiry Investigation Innovate Inquiry Definition: Pursuit of an answer to a question. Examples: Interviews and surveys will be conducted to answer the question: Why do people have their preferred social media platform? You’re searching for an answer to a question. Interviews are pieced together in a documentary to answer the question: Does being raised in a non-religious family within an otherwise predominantly religious area impact self-perception? Case studies should be examined to see if there is a correlation between a certain disease and a geographic location near the equator. Investigation Definition: A systematic and thorough attempt to learn the facts about something complex or hidden. Examples: Participants were shown different scenarios and asked about their observations to explore how banter as a communication act is received and why it’s received the way it is. Studying how a particular type of dance style can help reduce stress in children. You think a type of fungi native to Kentucky can cure cancer in mice, and you set up experiments to test your hypothesis. Innovate Definition: Introducing new ideas; original and creative thinking. Examples: Creating a new paint color that changes the color choices in hospice care or causes a shift in restaurant interior decorating because it’s seen as creating a comforting environment. Creating ceramic dishware depicting women’s achievements throughout history would not be original unless it has been done many times over. Creating a new form of computer coding. *All these contribute new knowledge to your fields if presented, published, or performed. Think about this, you could be: Observing something interesting and trying to understand and/or explain Identifying a need/challenge/opportunity and finding ways to solve it Posing an idea or question to pursue an answer Note: Classroom maintenance, office work, lab staffing, and assistance with classes/teaching are not considered research or creative inquiry. Undergraduate Research Fellowship Engage in research as early as your first year. Learn More Student Resources Student Resources Research resources for students. Faculty Resources Faculty Resources Resources for faculty research mentors. Opportunities for Students Opportunities for Students Opportunities to present and publish your research. Interest Form Interested in being engaged in research, but aren’t sure where to start? Fill out our interest form. The Coordinator of Undergraduate Research will reach out once the form has been completed and submitted. Interest Form Social Media Spotlight Have research experience? Want to be featured in the Center’s social media as part of our URF Spotlight? Social Media Spotlight Form Career Events SEE MORE MSU EVENTS CCDEE News Harr honored with Martin Visionary Award Harr honored with Martin Visionary Award Kentucky Commercialization Ventures presented Dr. Shannon Harr (Class of 1999, 2001) with the Thomas M. Martin Visionary A... Morehead State students recognized for community service Morehead State students recognized for community service More than 100 MSU students were named Spring 2026 Presidential Community Engaged Eagles for service-learning projects and ... Morehead State’s Alexis Mathews Selected for Nation... Morehead State’s Alexis Mathews Selected for Nation... MSU’s Alexis Mathews elected Division Representative for the Council on Undergraduate Research, advancing undergradu... Contact Us Alexis Mathews Coordinator of Undergraduate Research Camden-Carroll Library Morehead, KY 40351 EMAIL: armathews@moreheadstate.edu EMAIL: ugresearch@moreheadstate.edu PHONE: 606-783-2229 Apply Now Visit MSU Get More Info 150 University Blvd. Morehead, Kentucky 40351 1-800-585-6781 606-783-2000 Academic Catalogs Academic Calendars Accreditation Transcripts Privacy Policy Nondiscrimination & Title IX Web Accessibility MAKE A GIFT SEARCH JOB POSTINGS © 2026 Morehead State University"
    },
    "https://www.moreheadstate.edu/about-msu/leadership/administration/human-resources/careers": {
      "title": "CAREERS AT MSU",
      "description": "Careers at MSU | Morehead State University | Kentucky Skip Menu Menu Info For Current Students Future Students Craft Academy Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Parents & Families Community & Business Quicklinks MyMoreheadState Manage Your Account Blackboard Canvas Email Library Calendar of Events Search for Courses/Sections University Bookstore A-Z Guide Athletics Go Academics Explore Academic Programs Colleges & Departments Graduate Programs Online Programs Craft Academy for Excellence in Science & Mathematics George M. Luckey Academic Honors Program Academic Affairs & Provost Camden-Carroll Library Instructional Design & Online Learning Research Support & Success Career Prep Education Abroad Internships Level UP Service Learning Undergraduate Research Advising & Tutoring Essential Needs & Aid Student Accessibility Services Wellness & Emergency Resources Admissions & Aid Apply to MSU Transfer Eagle Scholars (Dual Credit) International Students Veteran & Military-Connected Students Financial Aid Scholarships Tuition & Fees Meet the Eagles - Student Stories Schedule a Visit Virtual Tour Student Life Activities & Organizations Athletics Housing Recreation & Wellness Center Dean of Students Eagle Student Handbook Campus Safety Student Center & Conference Services About MSU At-a-Glance History Mission & Vision Accreditation News Rankings Campus Map Emergency Resources Leadership Campus Revitalization Community & Business Contact Us Email Us! Home About Morehead State University Leadership Administration Human Resources Careers at MSU Section Menu Human Resources Careers at MSU Info for MSU Employees Student Employment Personnel Policies Forms & Documents HR Staff CAREERS AT MSU Morehead State University isn't just a workplace. Every day our faculty, staff and students work together to create a campus environment that promotes learning, support and achievement. We are committed to providing education and guidance to supervisors and potential employees regarding our processes, from job posting and recruitment to the application and selection of candidates. Hear from faculty and staff about their Morehead State experience. Join our MSU Team! Human Resources & Payroll provides a full range of personnel services for faculty, staff and external clients. Our goal is to ensure that the needs of the University and its employees are fully considered and met. We want to provide the best possible support for the betterment of Morehead State University, our faculty, staff and students. Career Opportunities View Job Postings Search Jobs Part-time & Temporary Employment View Info About MSU Morehead State University is a comprehensive public university located in Eastern Kentucky.  MSU aspires to be the best public regional university in the South through prioritizing student success; outcomes; academic excellence; and rankings, reputation and regional responsiveness. Explore MSU Forms & Documents View forms and documents for new and current employees. Wellness Program Learn more about MSU's wellness program for employees, Live Well, Work Well. Morehead-Rowan County Learn more about the community. Contact Human Resources Human Resources 301 Howell-McDowell Morehead, KY 40351 EMAIL: humanresources@moreheadstate.edu PHONE: 606-783-2097 View Human Resources Staff 150 University Blvd. Morehead, Kentucky 40351 1-800-585-6781 606-783-2000 Academic Catalogs Academic Calendars Accreditation Transcripts Privacy Policy Nondiscrimination & Title IX Web Accessibility MAKE A GIFT SEARCH JOB POSTINGS © 2026 Morehead State University"
    }
